      "side": 1,
      "message": "What happens if we accidentally have a different order in the devicetree? Something like:\n\n\tnamed-i2c-ports {\n\t\tcompatible \u003d \"named-i2c-ports\";\n\n\t\tpower {\n\t\t\ti2c-port \u003d \u003c\u0026i2c1\u003e;\n\t\t\t...\n\t\t};\n\t\tbattery {\n\t\t\ti2c-port \u003d \u003c\u0026i2c0\u003e;\n\t\t\t...\n\t\t};\n\t};\n\t\nHere, the first node is on port 1. Will that make a difference? It seems to me that this would set the physical port for `power` to 0 and `battery` to 1, but I\u0027m not finding anywhere that this would cause an error except for the print-out of the portmap.",
